  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 111 AM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures across the region are in the upper 50s \nto low 60s with winds out of the west to northwest around 10 mph. \nHigh pressure and quiet weather remain in place today through \nThursday. \n\nFriday morning brings the return of storm chances with an incoming \nlow pressure system. These storm chances are expected to last \nthrough the day and into early Saturday morning. MLCAPE Friday \nafternoon from the EC model is around 1500-2000 J/kg, falling to \nbetween 1200-1500 J/kg Friday evening. Lapse rates are around 7.5 \nC/km. SPC may put out an outlook for portions of the forecast area. \nSome 20-30% precipitation chances return Saturday evening. Limited \nprecipitation chances exist through the rest of the weekend into the \nmiddle of next work week with increasing chances Tuesday. These \nstorm chances are too far out to nail down severe potential.\n\nTemperatures will hover right around to slightly above average \nthrough the 7-day forecast. Smoke is pretty limited for the next few \ndays. Winds look to stay relatively light through the period.",
